.TH PKG-MANAGER-GUI 1 "2026-11-17" "pkg-manager-gui 1.1.0" "Mainuan"
.SH NAME
pkg-manager-gui \- graphical installer for Flatpak references and AppImage files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkg-manager-gui
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkg-manager-gui
chooses what to do from the file name:
.TP
.I *.flatpakref
The application is installed with
.BR flatpak (1),
or removed when an application with the same ID (the file name without
the extension) is already installed. When the user is not root and not a
member of the
.B flatpak
group, the command runs through
.BR pkexec (1).
.TP
.I *.AppImage
The file is copied to
.IR /opt/appimages-installed ,
with a menu entry and an icon, and recorded in the dpkg database as the
package
.IR <name> appimage,
or removed when that package is already installed. The work is done by
.I /usr/libexec/pkg-manager-gui/appimage_manager_backend
through
.BR pkexec (1)
(polkit action
.BR br.com.aratie.appimagemanager.pkexec ,
administrator authentication required).
.PP
A question confirms the installation or removal, a Qt window shows the
progress and a message box reports the result. Other files show a notice
that the format is not supported.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 1
when no file is given or the operation could not be started.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The interface follows
.BR LANGUAGE ,
.BR LC_ALL ,
.BR LC_MESSAGES " and " LANG .
.SH EXAMPLE
pkg-manager-gui ~/Downloads/org.gimp.GIMP.flatpakref
